Article 4

Every woman with disability, has the right to obtain:

a. education in all units, paths, types, and levels of education;
b. work and decent livelihood in accordance with the type and degree of disability, education, and ability;
c. equal treatment to play a role in development and enjoy the results;
d. accessibility in the context of independence; e. rehabilitation, social assistance, and maintenance of social welfare standards; and
f. equal rights to develop talents, abilities, and social life.

Article 23

(1) The implementation of protection for homeless women in order to provide protection and prevention against forms of violence caused by the absence of shelter or permanent residence.

(2) Homeless women as referred to in paragraph (1) obtain the right to protection for:

a. adequate housing;
b. health and social security;
c. population administration registration;
d. opportunity to obtain skills to improve economic status; and
e. access to information and legal consultation services.

Article 3

(1) Every woman has the right to:

a. live and maintain life and improve her standard of living;
b. fulfill her basic needs to grow and develop properly, have a family and continue descendants;
c. develop her personality, to obtain education, and improve her quality of life to become a faithful, pious, responsible, virtuous, happy, and prosperous human being in accordance with human rights;
d. obtain justice, security, and freedom to express opinions without discrimination;
e. be involved in every stage of the development process; f. be free from slavery or enslavement and threats;
g. obtain protection of personal self, family, honor, dignity and property rights;
h. obtain welfare and a decent life;
i. participate in politics;
j. perform legal acts;
k. freely choose a partner in marriage; and l. receive fair work wages in accordance with labor regulations.
(2) The right to participate in politics as referred to in paragraph (1) letter i is, women have the right to:
a. vote and/or be elected in general elections, regional head elections, or elections for political positions and other positions based on equal rights through direct, general, free, secret voting; and
b. be appointed to any government position. (3) Every woman who is in a condition of disability, elderly, and/or pregnant, has the right to obtain facilities and special treatment.
(4) Every elderly woman, person with physical disability and/or mental disability, has the right to obtain care, non-formal education.

Article 33

To provide Protection as referred to in Article 27, the City Regional Government may undertake efforts to:

a. provide services and handling as quickly as possible to witnesses and/or victims;
b. provide convenience, comfort, safety and free of charge for witnesses and/or victims;
c. maintain the confidentiality of witnesses and/or victims; d. guarantee justice and legal certainty for witnesses and/or victims;
e. provision of special service rooms at Police Offices;
f. provision of officers, health workers, social workers, and spiritual counselors;
g. creation and development of a system and mechanism for cooperation in service programs involving parties that are easily accessible to victims;
h. provide protection for companions, witnesses, family and friends of victims;
i. provide protection for female workers/laborers in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 27

(1) The implementation of protection for women victims of disasters in order to provide protection during disasters and post-disaster.

(2) Women victims of disasters as referred to in paragraph (1) obtain protection for:

a. access to adequate housing;
b. health services;
c. access to information services and legal consultation; and d. post-disaster recovery

